From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:09:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: export vkGetInstanceProcAddr and vkGetDeviceProcAddr

A program that dlopens the driver itself, with no Vulkan loader, looks
up these two by name. Wine's win32u does exactly that (vulkan_init_once:
dlsym of vkGetInstanceProcAddr and vkGetDeviceProcAddr), and on iOS
there is no loader for it to go through: the app embeds the driver as a
framework and win32u dlopens it. The ICD's own vk_icd* exports stay.

vkGetDeviceProcAddr answers as kk_GetDeviceProcAddr does, from the
device's exposed table. That table's command entry points are
KosmicKrisp's trampolines, which record a secondary command buffer's
commands so vkCmdExecuteCommands can replay them; the device's internal
table (vk_device_get_proc_addr) has none. Through it, DXVK's tiler mode,
which records every render pass into secondary command buffers, drew
nothing: Hollow Knight and The Witcher 3 showed only the DXVK HUD.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-vulkan-backend-build.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
index 90abd52..7100d5d 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
@@ -242,3 +242,27 @@ vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr(VkInstance instance, const char *pName)
 {
    return kk_GetInstanceProcAddr(instance, pName);
 }
+
+/* The two entry points a program that loads the driver itself, with no
+ * Vulkan loader, looks up by name. Wine's win32u does that on iOS (dlsym of
+ * vkGetInstanceProcAddr and vkGetDeviceProcAddr in the library it dlopens),
+ * where there is no loader to go through. Device entry points come from the
+ * device's exposed table, as kk_GetDeviceProcAddr gives them: its command
+ * trampolines record secondary command buffers for vkCmdExecuteCommands. */
+PUBLIC VKAPI_ATTR PFN_vkVoidFunction VKAPI_CALL
+vkGetInstanceProcAddr(VkInstance instance, const char *pName);
+
+PUBLIC VKAPI_ATTR PFN_vkVoidFunction VKAPI_CALL
+vkGetInstanceProcAddr(VkInstance instance, const char *pName)
+{
+   return vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr(instance, pName);
+}
+
+PUBLIC VKAPI_ATTR PFN_vkVoidFunction VKAPI_CALL
+vkGetDeviceProcAddr(VkDevice device, const char *pName);
+
+PUBLIC VKAPI_ATTR PFN_vkVoidFunction VKAPI_CALL
+vkGetDeviceProcAddr(VkDevice device, const char *pName)
+{
+   return kk_GetDeviceProcAddr(device, pName);
+}
